index a0c518c..076d369 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,7 +15,7 @@ even if you have no Java code.
 
 ## Kotlin version compatibility
 
-Any given release of scip-kotlin only supports one major version of Kotlin.
+This plugin uses compiler internals and must match the Kotlin compiler version.
 Use the table below to find the version of scip-kotlin that matches the Kotlin
 version you are using in your project.
 
@@ -23,6 +23,33 @@ version you are using in your project.
 |----------------|---------------------|
 | 1.8.x          | 0.3.2               |
 | 1.9.x          | 0.4.0               |
+| 2.1.20         | 0.5.0               |
+| 2.3.21         | 0.5.1-kotlin-2.3.21-SNAPSHOT (local build) |
+
+The compatibility patch adds the registrar plugin ID and updates FIR checker
+context parameters, containing-symbol lookup, and override lookup for Kotlin
+2.3.21. It preserves the earlier local/global symbol classification. Source
+streams are closed after reading, multi-line ranges use the end offset's line
+and column, and rendered documentation uses LF on Windows.
+
+Spotless 7.0.4 and ktfmt 0.55 support the context-parameter syntax. The
+formatter uses Kotlin style because ktfmt removed Dropbox style. CI installs
+JDK 8 and JDK 21, runs Gradle on 21, and checks formatting before tests.
+
+Build and run the regression suite with Gradle 8.10.2 using a JDK 17+ to run
+Gradle and a JDK 8 toolchain for the existing Java 8 output target:
+
+```powershell
+$env:OS = 'Windows_NT'
+./gradlew.bat --no-daemon '-Porg.gradle.java.installations.paths=C:/path/to/jdk8' spotlessCheck :semanticdb-kotlinc:test :semanticdb-kotlinc:shadowJar '-Pversion=0.5.1-kotlin-2.3.21-SNAPSHOT'
+```
+
+The suite includes an actual compiler invocation that checks emitted symbols,
+references and multi-line ranges. This patch was also verified with scip-java
+0.12.3 plus its Windows Gradle path-serialization fix against Moshi commit
+`889013ec2edb8d8034902662a1dc8c4f3b3f8111`, Kotlin 2.3.21 and Gradle 9.5.1.
+It does not establish compatibility with other Kotlin compiler versions and
+does not publish or replace an installed release automatically.
 
 ## SemanticDB support
 
@@ -75,3 +102,19 @@ If you have Coursier installed, you can run scip-java directly like this
 cd $SOURCEROOT_DIRECTORY
 ./coursier launch --contrib scip-java -- index-semanticdb TARGETROOT_DIRECTORY
 ```
+
+### Local scip-java integration
+
+Stage the versioned snapshot in a disposable Maven repository; this does not
+publish remotely or replace `0.5.0`:
+
+```powershell
+./gradlew.bat --no-daemon '-Porg.gradle.java.installations.paths=C:/path/to/jdk8' '-Pversion=0.5.1-kotlin-2.3.21-SNAPSHOT' '-Dmaven.repo.local=C:/path/to/disposable-maven' :semanticdb-kotlinc:publishShadowPublicationToMavenLocal
+```
+
+Build scip-java with `semanticdbKotlin = "0.5.1-kotlin-2.3.21-SNAPSHOT"`
+and `kotlinVersion = "2.3.21"` in `build.sbt`. Its existing Gradle plugin
+resolves from `mavenLocal()`. For the isolated generation process, set
+`JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS=-Dmaven.repo.local=C:/path/to/disposable-maven`.
+This compatibility build targets Kotlin 2.3.21; retain the released build for
+Kotlin 2.1.20. Do not overwrite an existing release coordinate.
